extend default

block vars
  - const page_title = 'Search for Workflows by ID or UUID';

block extrascripts
  block workscripts
    script(src = '/pages/search_workflowsByIDOrUUID.js')

block content
  .container-fluid
    .vert-space-x2
      h2 Search for Workflows by ID or UUID

    .vert-space-x1
      .panel.panel-default
      .foldable-heading.panel-heading.collapsed(data-toggle = 'collapse' data-target = '#descriptionBox')
        | Description: 
        i.chevron.fa.fa-fw 

      .collapse#descriptionBox
        p This page may be used to search for <b>workflows</b> using one of the following methods:
        ul
          li <b>by workflow ID</b>
          li <b>by the associated workflow component</b>, specified by its UUID

        p Each input box uses auto-complete - users may begin manually entering a workflow ID or component UUID, and up to 10 matching entries currently in the database will be displayed.  The auto-complete system is responsive - meaning that the list of displayed matches will be dynamically updated as more of the ID or UUID is entered.
          br
          |  The component UUID may alternatively be provided in full by scanning a component's QR code.  This can be done by simply pressing the 'camera' icon to the right of the UUID input box, and directing your device's camera view to the QR code in question.

        p At any time, if the ID corresponds to a single workflow record in the database, the user will be automatically redirected to the information page for the workflow.  If there is no corresponding record even after the entire ID has been provided, an error will be displayed.
          br
          |  Similarly, if the UUID corresponds to a single component record in the database, the user will be automatically redirected to the workflow information page.  If there is no corresponding record even after the entire UUID has been provided, an error will be displayed.

        p It should not be possible for multiple workflows to be associated with the same component, since each individual workflow begins with the creation of a new, unique component.  However, in the unlikely case of this situation occurring, a message will also be displayed indicating as such.

    .vert-space-x2 
      hr

      .row
        .col-md-4 
          h4 Search by Workflow ID

          .vert-space-x1
            p 
            | Enter a workflow ID below.<br>
            | &nbsp 

          .vert-space-x1
            #workflowidform

        .col-md-4
          h4 Search by Component UUID 

          .vert-space-x1
            p 
            | Enter a component UUID below.<br>
            | Alternatively, take a picture of the component's QR code.

          .vert-space-x1
            #componentuuidform

        .col-md-4

      .vert-space-x2 
        hr

      .vert-space-x1
        #messages

    .vert-space-x2
